==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 6~10 seconds<sup>180f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gory|Gories]] spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Fireworks Guys (High-Yield)]] spawn, delay 6~10 seconds<sup>180f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Fireworks Guys (Low-Yield)]] spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 6~10 seconds<sup>180f~300f</sup>.
*3 [[Bearkini]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.
*3 [[Teacher A]]s spawn after 93.33 seconds<sup>2,800f</sup>, delay 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*1 [[Teacher A]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**Infinite [[Bearkini]]s spawn, delay 53.33~56.67 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,700f</sup>.
**1 [[Bearkini]] spawns.
**5 [[Samurai Doggy|Samurai Doggies]] spawn, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
**2 [[Samurai Doggy|Samurai Doggies]] spawn, delay 4~6 seconds<sup>120f~180f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 50% HP:
**1 [[Gory Groom]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Gory Dark]]s spawn, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
**5 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
**5 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
**5 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
**8 [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**8 [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Standard meatshield tactics are effective against Teacher A and the Gorys. Remember that Teacher A has less range and damage than Master A. [[Axe Cat (Normal Cat)|Axe Cat]] or [[Swordsman Cat (Rare Cat)|Swordsman Cat]] can make mincemeat of the Samurai Doggy. Gory Groom is very tanky and hits hard, so you may need anti-Dark support units like [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Flower Cat]] or [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Cat Gunslinger]] to help your heavy-hitters.

